<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU fixes 265,000 T ACP, India sugar tariff quota.</title>
<headline>EU fixes 265,000 T ACP, India sugar tariff quota.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union agreed a reduced tariff quota of 265,000 tonnes of raw cane sugar from African, Caribbean and Pacific (ACP) countries and India between July 1 and February 28, 1998, an EU Commission official said.</p>
<p>Under the decision, taken by the EU sugar management committee on Wednesday, the ACP states will provide 255,000 tonnes and India 10,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The reduced duty was fixed at 5.41 Ecus per 100 kg of standard quality raw sugar, compared with 5.87 Ecus this season.</p>
<p>The minimum price for refiners was fixed at 49.68 Ecus per 100 kg effective from July 1.</p>
</text>
